  "repeatRecord": "docs/PRONUNCIATION-REPEATS.json",
  "method": "Single-reader-word groups retain their existing whole-word links. Shared groups require consensus across every literal source Hebrew reading and every exact path through documented reader letter forms. An explicit Hebrew maqaf/space part and transcription hyphen/space part correspond by source order. A unit gets one reader word ID only if the complete source part belongs to that same word on all matching paths. Combined source words retain group scope; alternate/missing cells and all text/IDs stay literal. No cap or approximate spelling distance.",
  "limits": "Structural source correspondence, not independent linguistic/acoustic approval. No phonemes, individual Hebrew-letter ranges, note links, audio times, new voice or Kinnor profile equivalence. All 68,354 original groups and their word links unchanged. Thirty groups use explicit UXLC written/read variants.119 further groups/141 words have primary MAM edition correspondence between unchanged old anchors; one further word has an explicitly documented MAM reading-form link. No Torah words remain without source-group correspondence; two words remain combined. Different spellings retain source-only ranges."
